  "THE_ONE_DISTRIBUTIONAL_CHANGE": {
   "what": "the request layer tints a fraction of DOOR cells, then hands the instance to the unchanged engine, solver and judge",
   "why": "maze_colour.generate zeroes the tint on start, goal, door and key cells, so a door cell is never tinted (measured: 160 door cells over 40 generator seeds, 0 tinted).  RULES A and B can then never interact WITHIN one transition, BLIND-SEQUENTIAL is vacuous at the transition level, and a transition instrument with no within-step interaction is not a composition instrument.",
   "legitimacy": "the RULES already specify the case -- judge, step, judge_ref and solve all resolve the door first and then test the tint against the UPDATED pocket.  Only the generator declines to emit it.  Same class of move as w9_maze.task._poison_pairs and _seal.",
   "safety": "every tinted instance is re-solved with the UNMODIFIED solver; a tint that kills the oracle is reverted",
